@base = https://cardboardtrade.xyz/v1
@owner = REPLACE_WITH_USER_WALLET
@authority = REPLACE_WITH_WALLET_OR_REGISTERED_SESSION
@builder = REPLACE_WITH_BUILDER_WALLET
@intent = REPLACE_WITH_PREPARED_INTENT_ID

### Public market data
GET {{base}}/accounts?kind=market

### Personal account balances; no signature needed
GET {{base}}/traders/{{owner}}

### Personal open/closed positions; a full 500-row page continues after its last address
GET {{base}}/positions/{{owner}}

### Builder earnings (integer USDC base units)
GET {{base}}/builders/{{builder}}/stats

### Builder positions; follow next_cursor for another page
GET {{base}}/builders/{{builder}}/positions?owner={{owner}}

### Ask for a wallet proof. Sign message or transaction using a wallet, not HTTP.
GET {{base}}/prepare-auth?owner={{owner}}&authority={{authority}}&lifetime_seconds=900

### Prepare a personal order. Replace expiry/signature using the challenge above.
POST {{base}}/prepare
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "owner": "{{owner}}",
  "authority": "{{authority}}",
  "admission": {"expires_at": 0, "signature": "REPLACE_WITH_BASE64_WALLET_SIGNATURE"},
  "action": "open", "market_id": 0, "margin": "10000000", "leverage": 10,
  "is_long": true, "debt_funded": false,
  "worst_price": "REPLACE_WITH_CURRENT_QUOTE_GUARD"
}

### Builder apps use the same prepare request, adding these three fields to its body:
# "builder_wallet": "{{builder}}"
# "builder_notional_markup_bps": 1000
# "builder_profit_markup_bps": 1000

### Submit only after wallet-signing the prepared transaction. Never retry blindly.
POST {{base}}/relay
Content-Type: application/json

{"id":"{{intent}}","transaction":"REPLACE_WITH_BASE64_SIGNED_WIRE"}

### Private status. Credential is base64(JSON {owner,authority,admission}).
GET {{base}}/transactions/{{intent}}
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_BASE64_CREDENTIAL
